        "notes": "Read all five steps and the exact density, rational Archimedean, inverse positivity, natural embedding and natural-addition order supplier statements/proofs. Definitions of real limits, sequences, real/rational identification, field, complete ordered field, absolute value and natural addition/order were checked. At k=0 the denominator is 1; N≥1 and k=N satisfy the tail chain. Only two existential witnesses for a fixed epsilon are used, with no AC. The rational-epsilon definition follows from a proof for every real epsilon; no converse is asserted. Current contract removes the impossible N=0 branch. Sources: Hunter Definition 3.10/Example 3.14, pp. 41–42; Lebl Definition 2.1.2/Example 2.1.4, pp. 52–53. No reader/refuter finding targets this example."
