          "source_section": "Example",
          "quote": "The sequence of reals $x_k := (k+1)^{-1}$, with $k+1 = \\sigma(k)$ the successor of $k$ read in $\\mathbb{R}$ through the canonical-natural embedding ([[lem-of-naturals-positive]]), converges to $0$ ([[def-real-limit]], [[def-sequence]]).",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "lem-nat-discrete",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For all $m, n \\in \\mathbb{N}$: $m < n \\iff \\sigma(m) \\le n$ ([[def-nat-order]]). Consequently there is no $k$ with $n < k < \\sigma(n)$: the successor $\\sigma(n)$ is the immediate successor of $n$.",
          "uses": [
            "2.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "def-nat-order",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "and the **strict order** by $m < n \\iff (m \\le n \\text{ and } m \\neq n)$, using addition ([[def-nat-addition]]).",
          "uses": [
            "2.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F5",
          "source": "lem-of-naturals-positive",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "- $n \\cdot 1_F > 0$ and $(n+1) \\cdot 1_F > n \\cdot 1_F$; - the map $n \\mapsto n \\cdot 1_F$ is strictly increasing, hence injective, on $\\{1, 2, 3, \\dots\\}$;",
          "uses": [
            "2.2",
            "2.3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F6",
          "source": "prop-of-reciprocal-order",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "$$0 < r < 1 \\iff \\tfrac{1}{r} > 1, \\qquad r > 1 \\iff 0 < \\tfrac{1}{r} < 1, \\qquad r = 1 \\iff \\tfrac{1}{r} = 1.$$",
          "uses": [
            "2.3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F7",
          "source": "lem-of-inverse-positive",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "1. If $a > 0$ then $a^{-1} > 0$. 2. If $0 < a < b$ then $0 < b^{-1} < a^{-1}$.",
          "uses": [
            "2.3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F8",
          "source": "def-abs-value",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "$$|x| \\;:=\\; \\begin{cases} x & \\text{if } x \\ge 0, \\\\ -x & \\text{if } x < 0. \\end{cases}$$",
          "uses": [
            "2.2",
            "2.3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F9",
          "source": "def-sequence",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "- $(x_k)$ is **bounded** if there is $M \\in \\mathbb{R}$ with $|x_k| \\le M$ for every $k \\in \\mathbb{N}$; it is **unbounded** otherwise.",
          "uses": [
