          "source": "def-divergence-to-infinity",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "- $(x_k)$ **diverges to $+\\infty$**, written $x_k \\to +\\infty$, when for every $M \\in \\mathbb{R}$ there is $K \\in \\mathbb{N}$ such that $x_k > M$ for all $k \\ge K$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "thm-of-archimedean",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Every complete ordered field $F$ ([[def-complete-ordered-field]]) is Archimedean: for every $x \\in F$ there is a natural number $n \\ge 1$ with $x < n \\cdot 1_F$, where $n \\cdot 1_F$ is the canonical natural of the ordered field $F$ ([[def-ordered-field]]).",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "lem-of-naturals-positive",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "- $n \\cdot 1_F > 0$ and $(n+1) \\cdot 1_F > n \\cdot 1_F$; - the map $n \\mapsto n \\cdot 1_F$ is strictly increasing, hence injective, on $\\{1, 2, 3, \\dots\\}$;",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "1.3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F5",
          "source": "lem-nat-order-add-compatible",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For all $m, n, k \\in \\mathbb{N}$: $m \\le n \\iff m + k \\le n + k$; and $m < n \\iff m + k < n + k$ ([[def-nat-order]]).",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F6",
          "source": "def-field",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "every $x \\ne 0$ has a multiplicative inverse $x^{-1}$ with $x \\cdot x^{-1} = 1$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F7",
          "source": "lem-null-times-bounded",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $(x_k)$ and $(y_k)$ be sequences of reals ([[def-sequence]]). If $(x_k)$ converges to $0$ ([[def-real-limit]]) and $(y_k)$ is bounded, then the product sequence $(x_k y_k)$ converges to $0$.",
          "uses": [
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F8",
          "source": "def-abs-value",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "$$|x| \\;:=\\; \\begin{cases} x & \\text{if } x \\ge 0, \\\\ -x & \\text{if } x < 0. \\end{cases}$$",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F9",
          "source": "def-real-limit",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "A sequence $(x_k)$ of reals **converges** to $x \\in \\mathbb{R}$ when for every rational $\\varepsilon > 0$ there is $K$ with $|x_k - x| < \\hat\\varepsilon$ for all $k \\ge K$.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F10",
          "source": "def-ordered-field",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "- **(O1) Trichotomy.** For each $x \\in F$, exactly one of the following holds: $x \\in P$, or $x = 0$, or $-x \\in P$.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F11",
          "source": "cor-of-one-positive",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "In any ordered field $F$ with positive cone $P$, the multiplicative identity satisfies $0 < 1$; that is, $1 \\in P$.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F12",
          "source": "lem-rat-embeds-dense",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "The map $q \\mapsto \\hat q$ ([[def-real-numbers]]) is an embedding of ordered fields.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F13",
          "source": "def-sequence",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "- $(x_k)$ is **bounded** if there is $M \\in \\mathbb{R}$ with $|x_k| \\le M$ for every $k \\in \\mathbb{N}$; it is **unbounded** otherwise.",
          "uses": [
            "3.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
