          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "- $(x_k)$ **diverges to $+\\infty$**, written $x_k \\to +\\infty$, when for every $M \\in \\mathbb{R}$ there is $K \\in \\mathbb{N}$ such that $x_k > M$ for all $k \\ge K$. - $(x_k)$ **diverges to $-\\infty$**, written $x_k \\to -\\infty$, when for every $M \\in \\mathbb{R}$ there is $K \\in \\mathbb{N}$ such that $x_k < M$ for all $k \\ge K$.",
