          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "It is refuted by the alternating sequence $(s_k)$ and the index map defined by $n_0 = 0$ and $n_{\\sigma(j)} = \\sigma(\\sigma(n_j))$: the refutation proves that $n$ is strictly increasing, $s_{n_j} = 1$ for every $j$, and $(s_k)$ does not converge.",
          "uses": [
            "1.3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "lem-of-abs-value",
          "source_section": "Statement",
