          "fact": "F5",
          "source": "lem-index-map-grows",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "If $n_i < n_{\\sigma(i)}$ for every $i \\in \\mathbb{N}$, then $n$ is strictly increasing.",
          "uses": [
            "1.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F6",
          "source": "def-sequence",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "A function $n : \\mathbb{N} \\to \\mathbb{N}$ is **strictly increasing** if $n_j < n_k$ whenever $j < k$. For such an $n$, the **subsequence** of $(x_k)$ along $n$ is the composite $x \\circ n$, written $(x_{n_k})_{k \\in \\mathbb{N}}$; it is again a sequence of reals.",
